& [CanonicalRecord: IR2FinalSlices] is the processed planning authority for IR2 final work slices
  + [canonical_uuid] is a54c15ea-4b50-4220-82e9-4cbba29201ce
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is b42d31c9-3da8-4f2f-909e-e6d16a21d57c
  + [slice_surface_uuid] is a98f03a1-5470-4fd9-bf01-736343ea191e
  + [authority_scope] is IR2 slice order, slice readiness, slice gates, model routing, expected outputs, verification oracles, implementation boundaries, and forbidden downstream scope
  + [implementation_scope] is authority-file parser and SQLite projection builder planning plus gated implementation slices
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/IR1_Implementation_Substrate_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR1_Scaffold_Creation_Review.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/schema/Kernel_Record_Core.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/schema/Authority_Kernel_Record_Schemas.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/schema/Natural_Key_And_Lifecycle_Matrix.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/decisions/Storage_Backend_Decision.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/slices/IR2_Final_Slices.v1.sop as the current IR2 slice surface
  = must: execute IR2-S01 first
  = must: run completion review after each IR2 slice before opening the next gated slice
  = must: preserve SOP files as authority and SQLite as derived, rebuildable projection
  = must: reject any output that treats generated SQLite, cache, index, extracted projection, or LangGraph checkpoint state as source authority
  - never: treat IR2 slice records as permission for operations control or live machine control

& [CanonicalIR2SliceSet] is the final IR2 slice sequence
  + [slice] is IR2-S01 parser and projection boundary and invariant map
  + [slice] is IR2-S02 SOP artifact discovery and parser profile contract
  + [slice] is IR2-S03 KernelRecord extraction and validation mapping
  + [slice] is IR2-S04 hash ledger, signature, and freshness validation contract
  + [slice] is IR2-S05 SQLite projection schema and rebuild policy
  + [slice] is IR2-S06 parser and projection implementation plan
  + [slice] is IR2-S07 parser/projection fixtures and expected-output ledgers
  + [slice] is IR2-S08 IR2 completion review and authority projection pack

  = must: preserve this order unless completion review rebakes IR2
  = must: mark downstream slices stale when an upstream accepted output changes

& [CanonicalIR2ExecutionGate] is the activation rule for IR2
  + [current_ready_slice] is IR2-S01
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-S02 until IR2-S01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-S03 until IR2-S02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-S04 until IR2-S03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-S05 until IR2-S04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-S06 until IR2-S05 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-S07 until IR2-S06 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR2-S08 until IR2-S07 accepted
  + [completion_gate] is IR2 authority projection pack accepted after IR2-S08

  = must: expose only IR2-S01 as ready right now
  = must: keep all later slices gated inside IR2

& [CanonicalIR2ModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR2-S01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR2-S02] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR2-S03] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR2-S04] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR2-S05] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR2-S06] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR2-S07] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR2-S01 through IR2-S06 are accepted and fixture scope is bounded
  + [IR2-S08] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: keep parser semantics, projection schema, source/projection boundary, and final activation under deeper reasoning
  = should: route bounded fixture records and expected-output ledgers to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark only after parser and projection contracts stabilize

